  "summary": "Duplicate Advisory: uv vulnerable to arbitrary file deletion through RECORD entries",
  "details": "## Duplicate Advisory\n\nThis advisory has been withdrawn because it is a duplicate of GHSA-pjjw-68hj-v9mw. This link is maintained to preserve external references.\n\n## Original Description\nAstral uv before 0.11.6 contains a path traversal vulnerability that allows attackers to delete arbitrary files by supplying wheels with relative traversal paths in RECORD entries. Attackers can craft a malicious wheel whose RECORD references files outside the installation prefix, causing uv to delete those files when the user uninstalls the package.",
